{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1356124-two-questions-for-a-setting-project","id":1356124,"title":"Two questions for a setting project","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-20T10:57:47-08:00","id":1356124,"title":"Two questions for a setting project","content":"I'm currently working on a film noir + weird horror setting. In this world magic exists but is legally regulated like firearms in the real world. My first question is how to go about using an existing merit, or creating a new one, for the lisence to practice magic legally. The magic system I have in mind is similar to the one in mage slightly modified. So if I allow mage magic to be taken as a merit would it make the pc more powerful than the other pcs to the point of dominating the game. If so any ideas on how to depower the mage without losing the flavor of the system? Like requiring merit dots in mage merit to increase arcana dots, or another way to slow their progress maybe? I'm open to any suggestions including not letting the pcs access magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T13:35:18-08:00","id":1356155,"title":"","content":"Have you considered using Proximi rules? They're based off the same magic system, but buy new Spells through Merit dots. As a result, they're much closer in power to baseline Mortals. Additionally, they get flavorful Curses, that generate Beats when they come into play. Officially published examples are present in:<br /> <br /> 